# Batch files must reach every PC with CRLF endings: cmd.exe mis-reads labels and
# "goto" in an LF-only .cmd/.bat (the updater's .bat once printed "'ld' is not recognized").
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# ...except the three that versions older than this file already have. Those versions check
# them out with the PC's own line endings, and both sides of a rollback must match:
# rollback.cmd rewrites itself and cmd resumes at the same byte offset, and a CRLF copy of an
# unchanged file shows up as a local edit on v1.2.x. So these keep the PC's own endings.
rollback.cmd !text !eol
install-updater.cmd !text !eol
updater/fpc-update-host.bat !text !eol
